{%- comment -%}
Base Homey recipe — every field the source exposes, ready to fork.

`homey` is the plugin_instance_select field keyname; TRMNL aliases the
installer's chosen Homey instance under it. A native Homey plugin exposes its
snapshot flat (`homey.devices`); a webhook source nests it (`homey.merge_variables.devices`).
`homey_data` below resolves to whichever is present, then exposes:

  homey_data.source          "companion" (push) or "cloud" (OAuth poll)
  homey_data.zone_names      { zoneId => zone name }
  homey_data.devices[]       name, zone, klass, available,
                             power (W), temperature (°C), humidity (%),
                             wind (km/h), energy (kWh),
                             titles { field => localized label },
                             on (true/false/null), alarms ["smoke", ...]
  homey_data.insight_title   } optional — present when a push producer
  homey_data.insight_unit    } includes a pre-fetched 24h series
  homey_data.insight_series  } [[timestamp, value], ...]

Aggregate in Liquid: filter with `where`/`where_exp`, order with `sort`,
sum with a `plus` loop. Liquid cannot build arrays — aggregate where you render.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign homey_data = homey.merge_variables | default: homey -%}
{%- assign devices = homey_data.devices -%}
{% if devices == blank %}
  <div class="layout layout--col gap flex flex--center">
    <span class="label label--gray">Waiting for the first push from Homey…</span>
  </div>
  <div class="title_bar">
    <span class="title">Homey</span>
    <span class="instance">Not connected</span>
  </div>
{% else %}
  {%- assign zones = devices | map: "zone" | uniq -%}
  <div class="layout layout--col gap">
    {% for zone in zones limit: 3 %}
      {% render "homey_zone_section", devices: devices, zone: zone %}
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  <div class="title_bar">
    <span class="title">Homey</span>
    <span class="instance">{{ zones | size }} zones &middot; {{ devices | size }} devices</span>
  </div>
{% endif %}
